  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a balanced compromise: S2 adopts Halcyon's 5% thermal-test maximum with a 12-month remediation window for existing models, while S5 adopts Northwind's 8/100k mandatory recall trigger, which catches Halcyon's Ember 8. Northwind secures a 72-month remote-shutoff retrofit deadline and avoids public per-model failure-rate disclosure; Halcyon secures customer access to per-model results and a 36-month lead time for built-in fire suppression. S1 is strict on reporting, including reporting while cause is unknown."
